    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d417">

                <pb facs="0448" n="442" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg442"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Taylor to Mr.
                            Gresham</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 140.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-03-08"><hi rendition="#italic">March 8, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received March 26.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In my No. 135, of the 2d instant, I
                    informed you of the promise of the minister of state to summon me in a few days
                    for the discussion of the proposed convention. Yesterday I received a personal
                    note, a copy of which I inclose with translation, in which he requests a delay
                    until the termination of the pending cabinet crisis. It seems to be certain that
                    the present cabinet will be reorganized in a very few days, after the withdrawal
                    of several members. As soon as the reorganization is effected I will press the
                    convention for discussion. In the meantime it is useless to attempt
                    anything.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hannis Taylor.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d417-a1.xml" xpointer="d417-a1"/>
            </div>
